s Created\n\n**Start here:**\n- **`README-SETUP.md`** — Overview and quick start guide\n- **`quick-setup.sh`** — One-command setup on your server\n\n**Reference:**\n- **`GIT-DEPLOY-SETUP.md`** — Detailed documentation with architecture\n- **`setup-git-server.sh`** — Just git repository setup\n- **`setup-web-server.sh`** — Just web server setup\n- **`web-server.service`** — Systemd service for persistent web server\n\n## How It Works\n\nThe system uses a **post-receive hook** in a bare git repository. When you push:\n\n```\ngit push → /git/server (bare repo) → post-receive hook → /var/www/html (web root) → served on :8080\n```\n\n## Quick Setup on Your Server\n\n```bash\n# Run the setup script\n./quick-setup.sh\n\n# Start the web server (pick one):\n\n# Easy option - Python (no installation):\ncd /var/www/html && python3 -m http.server 8080\n\n# Persistent option - systemd:\nsudo cp web-server.service /etc/systemd/system/\nsudo systemctl start web-server\nsudo systemctl enable web-server\n```\n\n## Then From Your Computer\n\n```bash\ngit clone ssh://user@server/git/server my-project\ncd my-project\necho \"hello world\" > hello.html\ngit add hello.html\ngit commit -m \"add hello.html\"\ngit push origin master\n\n# It's live!\ncurl http://server:8080/hello.html\n# → hello world\n```\n\nThe hook handles the deployment automatically — no additional scripts or manual steps needed. All files in your repository become accessible on the web server immediately after you push.","ttft_ms":4740,"type":"result","duration_ms":64255,"uuid":"6cd29c7e-da45-44fc-9021-dcf2f6fcc7bc","ttft_stream_ms":935,"time_to_request_ms":75,"queued_turn_count":0}
